    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/kutztownedu/jobs/5474307/temporary-part-time-instructor-in-sociology": {
      "title": "Temporary, Part-Time Instructor in Sociology",
      "description": "Temporary, Part-Time Instructor in Sociology Location Kutztown, PA Job Type Temporary Part Time Job Number AY 26.27 1125B Division Academic Affairs Department Society, History and Culture Opening Date 09/08/2026 Closing Date Continuous Bargaining Unit APSCUF Classification APSCUF Description Benefits Questions Job Summary Kutztown University of Pennsylvania enrolls approximately 7,500 students across its graduate and undergraduate programs. Located in a charming rural setting in Kutztown, Pennsylvania, the University is just a 20-minute drive from the metropolitan areas of Allentown/Bethlehem and Reading, and about an hour from the Philadelphia metropolitan area. The University seeks to hire employees with experience working with diverse populations. The Department of Society, History, and Culture seeks a part-time Sociologist at the Instructor level to teach two classes in Spring 2027. The successful candidate will have teaching experience with courses commensurate with the department's needs. Experience teaching in one or more of the following areas is preferred: medical sociology, sociology of education, race and ethnicity, social problems, family, and gender. In accordance with the Collective Bargaining Agreement, performance review and evaluation of faculty is based on effective teaching and fulfillment of professional responsibilities; continuing scholarly growth; and service. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Minimum Qualifications - Master's Degree in Sociology or related social science interdisciplinary field - One year of teaching experience - Availability to teach classes in person Preferred Qualifications - Ph.D. in Sociology Supplemental Information Applicants should submit the following materials through NeoEd: (a) letter of interest; (b) a current curriculum vitae; (c) teaching evaluations; (d) unofficial transcripts; and (e) contact information for three (3) professional ref